              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jenn N."
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a great recipe and very easy. I used ground venison instead of beef, added alittle extra garlic, topped with mexican cheese and sour cream. it will definately be a regular chili recipe in my house."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "France C"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The tequila is undetectable, so I’d just leave it out, or drink it instead! The onion doesn’t have enough time to cook down in 20. I had to go an extra 15. I’d just add the onion to the meat mixture next time to get it started. This is very meaty and thick, so if you like a little more liquid in your chili, I’d add another can of tomato sauce, or some broth. A decent basic chili, however I missed the layers of flavor that other chilis have. I served it with cheese, sour cream, green onion. I also used fire roasted tomatoes instead of Italian stewed.",
            "datePublished": "2021-08-12T01:36:05.477Z"
          },
          {
